WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.308
Royal Crest Academy presents, hackathons, and science exhibitions.

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:06.441
Hackathon.

3
00:00:06.491 --> 00:00:08.331
A short, intense team challenge.

4
00:00:08.381 --> 00:00:10.575
You get a real problem and a deadline,

5
00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:13.787
then you design, code and build a working solution.

6
00:00:15.137 --> 00:00:16.169
Science exhibition.

7
00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:20.098
A showcase where students display experiments, models and inventions,

8
00:00:20.148 --> 00:00:22.975
and explain the science to visitors and judges.

9
00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:26.898
Every field has its own colour code.

10
00:00:26.948 --> 00:00:27.918
Physics, blue.

11
00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:29.011
Chemistry, red.

12
00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:30.104
Biology, green.

13
00:00:30.154 --> 00:00:31.561
Mathematics, purple.

14
00:00:31.611 --> 00:00:33.236
Computer science, teal.

15
00:00:33.286 --> 00:00:35.641
Technical and vocational, yellow.

16
00:00:35.691 --> 00:00:37.735
And arts and design, pink.

17
00:00:39.235 --> 00:00:40.766
Stage one: the opening ceremony.

18
00:00:40.816 --> 00:00:43.042
Teams meet, and the challenge is revealed.

19
00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:44.686
The doors open.

20
00:00:46.742 --> 00:00:49.131
And every great project begins with research.

21
00:00:50.481 --> 00:00:52.217
Stage two: the hackathon.

22
00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.418
Now, we build.

23
00:00:53.818 --> 00:00:55.460
Designers plan to scale,

24
00:00:57.118 --> 00:00:58.984
engineers wire their own drones,

25
00:01:00.418 --> 00:01:02.185
coders test every circuit,

26
00:01:03.718 --> 00:01:06.281
a motor and some copper wire become a robot,

27
00:01:07.381 --> 00:01:09.198
and cardboard starts to move.

28
00:01:10.681 --> 00:01:11.925
And when it finally works?

29
00:01:11.975 --> 00:01:13.468
That feeling is everything.

30
00:01:14.818 --> 00:01:17.082
Stage three: the science exhibition.

31
00:01:17.482 --> 00:01:19.399
Chemists filter and evaporate,

32
00:01:20.782 --> 00:01:23.171
and grow crystals they can hold in their hands.

33
00:01:25.782 --> 00:01:28.619
Physicists control the current with a rheostat,

34
00:01:29.719 --> 00:01:31.312
model the solar system,

35
00:01:33.019 --> 00:01:35.159
and guide light through fibre optics.

36
00:01:36.319 --> 00:01:38.858
Computer scientists fly by live video,

37
00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:42.322
above a smart city they built themselves.

38
00:01:43.422 --> 00:01:46.184
Designers turn African wax print into fashion,

39
00:01:47.284 --> 00:01:49.599
and artists bring every idea to life.

40
00:01:50.949 --> 00:01:52.989
Stage four: the closing ceremony.

41
00:01:53.599 --> 00:01:55.739
Every team pitches to the judges,

42
00:01:56.899 --> 00:01:59.064
and the boldest ideas take the trophy.

43
00:02:00.199 --> 00:02:03.450
It's in our prospectus: six disciplines taught by specialists,

44
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.271
the ZIMSEC syllabus with Cambridge-aligned standards,

45
00:02:06.321 --> 00:02:08.335
and clubs like Robotics and Coding.

46
00:02:09.785 --> 00:02:11.079
Royal Crest Academy.

47
00:02:11.129 --> 00:02:12.893
Science, innovation, skill.

48
00:02:12.943 --> 00:02:16.454
Opening on the first of January, twenty twenty-seven.

49
00:02:16.504 --> 00:02:17.059
Think it.

50
00:02:17.109 --> 00:02:17.664
Build it.

51
00:02:17.714 --> 00:02:18.468
Prove it.
